# User-Facing Messages — Russian

## Requirement

All messages visible to the user must be in **Russian**.

## Scope

### Frontend (apps/web)

- Toast notifications
- Form validation messages
- Error states and empty states
- Button labels, placeholders (unless coming from design system)
- Any text shown to the end user

### Backend (apps/api)

- Error messages in API responses (e.g. `UnauthorizedException`, `BadRequestException`)
- Auth-related errors (invalid credentials, token expired, account disabled)
- Validation error messages from DTOs or Zod
- Any message that the frontend will display to the user

## Why

- Target audience is Russian-speaking
- Backend messages are often shown as-is on the frontend (e.g. in toasts or error banners)
- Consistent language across the product

## Examples

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — backend
throw new UnauthorizedException('Invalid credentials');

// ✅ GOOD — backend
throw new UnauthorizedException('Неверный email или пароль');
```

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — frontend
toast.error('Something went wrong');

// ✅ GOOD — frontend
toast.error('Что-то пошло не так');
```
